    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30992" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ninnius</span></b> , a, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a noble Campanian</i>
			gens, <i><span class="en">Liv.
				23, 8</span></i>.—So, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> L. Ninnius Quadratus, <i>a tribune of the
				people</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 3, 23, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Sest.
				31, 68</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Ninnius Crassus, <i>who translated the Iliad
				into Latin</i>, <i><span class="en">Prisc. 865</span></i> P.;
			cf. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 475, 14</span></i>.</div>
